                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "47b621aa-6d08-377b-b566-a09579741159",
                        "entry_id": "9cf5d7fb-c89c-307e-9d37-d0ac0d1a2e3d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "выпускание из организма некоторого количества крови с лечебной целью"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40db749f-740f-48b6-ae6e-294f491a92f3",
                                "sense_id": "47b621aa-6d08-377b-b566-a09579741159",
                                "text": "Пришли к мысли, что раньше, во времена их детства, на постоялых дворах, в гостиницах клопы производили кровопускание, вводили в кровь антикоагулянты, и инсультов было меньше."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93c29851-4c43-3d45-bb4f-4d8131d1212e",
                        "entry_id": "9cf5d7fb-c89c-307e-9d37-d0ac0d1a2e3d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. о массовых убийствах, войне"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8194fd74-ee49-454a-b243-1ed103dad208",
                                "sense_id": "93c29851-4c43-3d45-bb4f-4d8131d1212e",
                                "text": "Его идеалы обветшали, к тому же утомился сам Запад, устроивший себе колоссальное кровопускание в виде двух мировых войн."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "051eeadf-cf0a-44b8-b1fe-1d6d0c83801f",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cf5d7fb-c89c-307e-9d37-d0ac0d1a2e3d",
                        "target_lang_word": "phlebotomy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "phlebotomy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                        "entry_id": "b470655d-b9a6-311d-ae69-94d1e3bd4ff4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The opening of a vein, either to withdraw blood or for letting blood; venesection."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be150b70-1065-4e99-9773-0fe8a7aba29e",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Now butter with a leafe of Sage is good to Parge the bloud, Fly Venus and Phlebotomy for they are neither good."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "883908b0-2347-48f4-b419-3920557a526e",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Phlebotomy is promiscuously used before and after physick, commonly before and upon occasion is often reiterated, if there be any need at least of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd48cdf8-9157-479f-990e-0482602d9846",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "He had even taken from his pocket a cupping apparatus, and was about to proceed to phlebotomy, when the object of his anxious solicitude suddenly revived […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec84433f-c3d3-4803-b1c9-c0187a3f6a24",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Of course, members of the family were foremost in spilling loyal blood on Marston Moor, that great field of plebotomy to so may Cavaliers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "340002a6-0c29-4694-bc36-1c0b31720c62",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Then she made an impatient gesture with her hand. \"Time was, my dear colleague, when a snuff-box was as much part of my equipment as my phlebotomy case.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "adab177e-42d7-445b-abde-c976068764b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cf5d7fb-c89c-307e-9d37-d0ac0d1a2e3d",
                        "target_lang_word": "bloodletting",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bloodletting",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11e3c5ee-e49f-3bcf-9554-68550175adca",
                                        "entry_id": "2dbbaf7d-89d8-3ebf-bbc4-9ca937a900ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The archaic practice of treating illness by removing some blood, believed to be tainted, from the stricken person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c80de104-fe82-41cf-b3bc-47940cbfe3a9",
                                                "sense_id": "11e3c5ee-e49f-3bcf-9554-68550175adca",
                                                "text": "The pungent pain, dyspnœa, cephalalgia, redness of the face, pulsations of the heart, strong and rapid, the pulse full and vibrating, induced M. Peyrade, then attached to that hospital, to practise blood-letting in the arm. It was followed with marked relief."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c48afc83-e6ff-354e-92f7-28652d2f0d2d",
                                        "entry_id": "2dbbaf7d-89d8-3ebf-bbc4-9ca937a900ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The diminishment of any resource with the hope that this will lead to a positive effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7544283-dbf4-4bf4-a8fe-e30fce0bb01b",
                                                "sense_id": "c48afc83-e6ff-354e-92f7-28652d2f0d2d",
                                                "text": "Yet another round of corporate bloodletting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fed36a7-a55e-47a7-bb0a-3dbb053b9562",
                                                "sense_id": "c48afc83-e6ff-354e-92f7-28652d2f0d2d",
                                                "text": "Only when the bankers and industrialists abroad realized that a ferocious class struggle in Germany was raging did they begin to relent somewhat on their economic bloodletting."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38982ea0-d393-3166-9eff-9b73424e09e2",
                                        "entry_id": "2dbbaf7d-89d8-3ebf-bbc4-9ca937a900ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A circumstance, such as a battle, where a large amount of blood is likely to be spilled through violence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ec952f2-81d9-439a-94a9-2c02ed5cd86c",
                                                "sense_id": "38982ea0-d393-3166-9eff-9b73424e09e2",
                                                "text": "In 1856 Tu Wen-hsiu rose up in rebellion and occupied Ta-li.[...]\"The conflict between the Han Chinese and the Moslems began over trifles. It has developed into a tragedy of mutual bloodletting because of poor management by the civil and military officials at Yung-ch'ang county and of Yunnan province. As a result, the mutual killing spread throughout Yunnan. The fault lies not with the people but with the officials.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
